  "rationale": "Reasoning: Select the best direct-match PRS for cervical carcinoma based on phenotype alignment and relative validation performance versus the provided performance landscape. Evidence: All 6 candidates directly match the target trait (trait_efo=cervical carcinoma; trait_reported=Cervical cancer). PGS001299 reports the highest discrimination (AUC=0.91431) with a large training sample (n=269,704) and validation sample (n=67,425), and its AUC is far above the landscape p75 (0.6752) and near the upper end of reported AUCs (max 0.98137). Other models have substantially lower AUCs (0.563–0.745) despite some having larger GWAS variant sample sizes (e.g., PGS003428 samples_variants n=326,610 but AUC=0.613). PGS001299 also includes multi-ancestry evaluation (AFR/EAS/EUR/SAS), which is broader than the EUR-only evaluations of several alternatives. Recommendation: Treat this as a direct high-quality match and prioritize PGS001299 as the best available direct model for cervical carcinoma in this candidate set. Caveats: Confidence is Moderate because (i) AUC comparability across studies can be affected by differing phenotyping (e.g., incident vs. prevalent), covariate adjustment, and evaluation design; (ii) PGS001299 uses a relatively small variant count (24) despite high AUC, which warrants scrutiny for potential overfitting or cohort-specific effects; (iii) some metrics are missing/inconsistent across models (many r2 missing), limiting multi-metric comparison."
}

